WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Why do I know better,

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.580
yet still sin?

3
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.700
Romans seven shows us something painful:

4
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.560
knowing the command does not give us

5
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.960
the power to obey it.

6
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.660
God’s law is holy and good.

7
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.360
It exposes sin,

8
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.700
including the desires we would rather leave

9
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.180
unnamed.

10
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.440
But a diagnosis cannot heal the disease.

11
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.260
Paul’s cry is,

12
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.880
who will deliver me?

13
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.580
His answer points us to Jesus Christ.

14
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.300
Romans eight says God has done what

15
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:32.840
the law,

16
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.200
weakened by the flesh,

17
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.200
could not do.

18
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:36.720
He sent his Son.

19
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.160
When Scripture exposes your sin,

20
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.720
be honest about it.

21
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:41.880
Bring it to Christ.

22
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.660
Your hope for rescue rests in him,

23
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.460
even when you feel the depth

24
00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.100
of your need.
